  "reason": "No completed experiments provide evidence, so the priority is to establish a simple, low-risk baseline and reduce uncertainty about whether basic RNA profiling alone is informative. config_001 tests a minimal RNA-only single-profile model with a standard PCA representation, clarifying the reference performance of the RNA branch before adding complexity. It is the best first experiment under a limited budget because it is simple, interpretable, and provides an anchor for later comparisons of multiprofile aggregation, learned RNA encoders, image modality, and multimodal fusion."
